<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>OCM CLI on Open Component Model</title><link>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/</link><description>Recent content in OCM CLI on Open Component Model</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-US</language><atom:link href="https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>ocm</title><link>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="ocm"&gt;ocm&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The official Open Component Model (OCM) CLI&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="synopsis"&gt;Synopsis&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The Open Component Model command line client supports the work with OCM&#10;artifacts, like Component Archives, Common Transport Archive,&#10;Component Repositories, and Component Versions.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>ocm add</title><link>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-add/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-add/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="ocm-add"&gt;ocm add&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Add anything to OCM&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;div class="expressive-code"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figure class="frame not-content"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figcaption class="header"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;span class="title"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;ocm add {component-version|component-versions|cv|cvs} [flags]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;h3 id="options"&gt;Options&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;div class="expressive-code"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figure class="frame not-content"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figcaption class="header"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;span class="title"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt; -h, --help help for add&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;h3 id="options-inherited-from-parent-commands"&gt;Options inherited from parent commands&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;div class="expressive-code"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figure class="frame not-content"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figcaption class="header"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;span class="title"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt; --config stringArray supply configuration by a given configuration file.&#10; By default (without specifying custom locations with this flag), the file will be read from one of the well known locations:&#10; 1. The path specified in the OCM_CONFIG environment variable&#10; 2. The XDG_CONFIG_HOME directory (if set), or the default XDG home ($HOME/.config), or the user&amp;#39;s home directory&#10; - $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ocm/config&#10; - $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/.ocmconfig&#10; - $HOME/.config/ocm/config&#10; - $HOME/.config/.ocmconfig&#10; - $HOME/.ocm/config&#10; - $HOME/.ocmconfig&#10; 3. The current working directory:&#10; - $PWD/.ocm/config&#10; - $PWD/.ocmconfig&#10; 4. The directory of the current executable:&#10; - $EXE_DIR/.ocm/config&#10; - $EXE_DIR/.ocmconfig&#10; If multiple configuration files are found, they will be merged in the order they are discovered.&#10; Later entries have higher priority.&#10; Using the option, the specified configuration file(s) will be used instead of the lookup above.&#10; --logformat enum set the log output format that is used to print individual logs&#10; json: Output logs in JSON format, suitable for machine processing&#10; text: Output logs in human-readable text format, suitable for console output&#10; (must be one of [json text]) (default text)&#10; --loglevel enum sets the logging level&#10; debug: Show all logs including detailed debugging information&#10; info: Show informational messages and above&#10; warn: Show warnings and errors only (default)&#10; error: Show errors only&#10; (must be one of [debug error info warn]) (default info)&#10; --logoutput enum set the log output destination&#10; stdout: Write logs to standard output&#10; stderr: Write logs to standard error, useful for separating logs from normal output&#10; (must be one of [stderr stdout]) (default stderr)&#10; --plugin-directory string default directory path for ocm plugins. (default &amp;#34;$HOME/.config/ocm/plugins&amp;#34;)&#10; --plugin-shutdown-timeout duration Timeout for plugin shutdown. If a plugin does not shut down within this time, it is forcefully killed (default 10s)&#10; --temp-folder string Specify a custom temporary folder path for filesystem operations.&#10; --working-directory string Specify a custom working directory path to load resources from.&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;h3 id="see-also"&gt;SEE ALSO&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm/"&gt;ocm&lt;/a&gt;&#9; - The official Open Component Model (OCM) CLI&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-add-component-version/"&gt;ocm add component-version&lt;/a&gt;&#9; - Add component version(s) to an OCM Repository based on a &amp;ldquo;component-constructor&amp;rdquo; file&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;</description></item><item><title>ocm add component-version</title><link>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-add-component-version/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-add-component-version/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="ocm-add-component-version"&gt;ocm add component-version&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Add component version(s) to an OCM Repository based on a &amp;ldquo;component-constructor&amp;rdquo; file&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="synopsis"&gt;Synopsis&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Add component version(s) to an OCM repository that can be reused for transfers.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>ocm completion</title><link>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-completion/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-completion/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="ocm-completion"&gt;ocm completion&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="synopsis"&gt;Synopsis&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Generate the autocompletion script for ocm for the specified shell.&#10;See each sub-command&amp;rsquo;s help for details on how to use the generated script.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>ocm completion bash</title><link>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-completion-bash/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-completion-bash/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="ocm-completion-bash"&gt;ocm completion bash&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Generate the autocompletion script for bash&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="synopsis"&gt;Synopsis&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Generate the autocompletion script for the bash shell.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This script depends on the &amp;lsquo;bash-completion&amp;rsquo; package.&#10;If it is not installed already, you can install it via your OS&amp;rsquo;s package manager.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>ocm completion fish</title><link>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-completion-fish/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-completion-fish/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="ocm-completion-fish"&gt;ocm completion fish&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Generate the autocompletion script for fish&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="synopsis"&gt;Synopsis&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Generate the autocompletion script for the fish shell.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;To load completions in your current shell session:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>ocm completion powershell</title><link>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-completion-powershell/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-completion-powershell/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="ocm-completion-powershell"&gt;ocm completion powershell&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Generate the autocompletion script for powershell&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="synopsis"&gt;Synopsis&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Generate the autocompletion script for powershell.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;To load completions in your current shell session:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>ocm completion zsh</title><link>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-completion-zsh/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-completion-zsh/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="ocm-completion-zsh"&gt;ocm completion zsh&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Generate the autocompletion script for zsh&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="synopsis"&gt;Synopsis&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Generate the autocompletion script for the zsh shell.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;If shell completion is not already enabled in your environment you will need&#10;to enable it. You can execute the following once:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>ocm describe</title><link>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-describe/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-describe/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="ocm-describe"&gt;ocm describe&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Describe OCM entities or metadata&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;div class="expressive-code"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figure class="frame not-content"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figcaption class="header"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;span class="title"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;ocm describe [flags]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;h3 id="options"&gt;Options&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;div class="expressive-code"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figure class="frame not-content"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figcaption class="header"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;span class="title"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt; -h, --help help for describe&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;h3 id="options-inherited-from-parent-commands"&gt;Options inherited from parent commands&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;div class="expressive-code"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figure class="frame not-content"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figcaption class="header"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;span class="title"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt; --config stringArray supply configuration by a given configuration file.&#10; By default (without specifying custom locations with this flag), the file will be read from one of the well known locations:&#10; 1. The path specified in the OCM_CONFIG environment variable&#10; 2. The XDG_CONFIG_HOME directory (if set), or the default XDG home ($HOME/.config), or the user&amp;#39;s home directory&#10; - $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ocm/config&#10; - $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/.ocmconfig&#10; - $HOME/.config/ocm/config&#10; - $HOME/.config/.ocmconfig&#10; - $HOME/.ocm/config&#10; - $HOME/.ocmconfig&#10; 3. The current working directory:&#10; - $PWD/.ocm/config&#10; - $PWD/.ocmconfig&#10; 4. The directory of the current executable:&#10; - $EXE_DIR/.ocm/config&#10; - $EXE_DIR/.ocmconfig&#10; If multiple configuration files are found, they will be merged in the order they are discovered.&#10; Later entries have higher priority.&#10; Using the option, the specified configuration file(s) will be used instead of the lookup above.&#10; --logformat enum set the log output format that is used to print individual logs&#10; json: Output logs in JSON format, suitable for machine processing&#10; text: Output logs in human-readable text format, suitable for console output&#10; (must be one of [json text]) (default text)&#10; --loglevel enum sets the logging level&#10; debug: Show all logs including detailed debugging information&#10; info: Show informational messages and above&#10; warn: Show warnings and errors only (default)&#10; error: Show errors only&#10; (must be one of [debug error info warn]) (default info)&#10; --logoutput enum set the log output destination&#10; stdout: Write logs to standard output&#10; stderr: Write logs to standard error, useful for separating logs from normal output&#10; (must be one of [stderr stdout]) (default stderr)&#10; --plugin-directory string default directory path for ocm plugins. (default &amp;#34;$HOME/.config/ocm/plugins&amp;#34;)&#10; --plugin-shutdown-timeout duration Timeout for plugin shutdown. If a plugin does not shut down within this time, it is forcefully killed (default 10s)&#10; --temp-folder string Specify a custom temporary folder path for filesystem operations.&#10; --working-directory string Specify a custom working directory path to load resources from.&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;h3 id="see-also"&gt;SEE ALSO&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm/"&gt;ocm&lt;/a&gt;&#9; - The official Open Component Model (OCM) CLI&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-describe-types/"&gt;ocm describe types&lt;/a&gt;&#9; - Describe OCM types and their configuration schema&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;</description></item><item><title>ocm describe types</title><link>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-describe-types/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-describe-types/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="ocm-describe-types"&gt;ocm describe types&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Describe OCM types and their configuration schema&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="synopsis"&gt;Synopsis&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Describe OCM types registered in various subsystems.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;WHAT ARE SUBSYSTEMS?&#10;OCM uses a plugin-based architecture where different types of functionality are organized&#10;into subsystems. Each subsystem is a collection of related type implementations. When you&#10;use OCM commands or configure OCM resources, you specify types from these subsystems.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>ocm download</title><link>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-download/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-download/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="ocm-download"&gt;ocm download&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Download anything from OCM&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;div class="expressive-code"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figure class="frame not-content"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figcaption class="header"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;span class="title"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;ocm download {resource|resources|plugin|plugins} [flags]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;h3 id="options"&gt;Options&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;div class="expressive-code"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figure class="frame not-content"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figcaption class="header"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;span class="title"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt; -h, --help help for download&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;h3 id="options-inherited-from-parent-commands"&gt;Options inherited from parent commands&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;div class="expressive-code"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figure class="frame not-content"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figcaption class="header"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;span class="title"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt; --config stringArray supply configuration by a given configuration file.&#10; By default (without specifying custom locations with this flag), the file will be read from one of the well known locations:&#10; 1. The path specified in the OCM_CONFIG environment variable&#10; 2. The XDG_CONFIG_HOME directory (if set), or the default XDG home ($HOME/.config), or the user&amp;#39;s home directory&#10; - $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ocm/config&#10; - $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/.ocmconfig&#10; - $HOME/.config/ocm/config&#10; - $HOME/.config/.ocmconfig&#10; - $HOME/.ocm/config&#10; - $HOME/.ocmconfig&#10; 3. The current working directory:&#10; - $PWD/.ocm/config&#10; - $PWD/.ocmconfig&#10; 4. The directory of the current executable:&#10; - $EXE_DIR/.ocm/config&#10; - $EXE_DIR/.ocmconfig&#10; If multiple configuration files are found, they will be merged in the order they are discovered.&#10; Later entries have higher priority.&#10; Using the option, the specified configuration file(s) will be used instead of the lookup above.&#10; --logformat enum set the log output format that is used to print individual logs&#10; json: Output logs in JSON format, suitable for machine processing&#10; text: Output logs in human-readable text format, suitable for console output&#10; (must be one of [json text]) (default text)&#10; --loglevel enum sets the logging level&#10; debug: Show all logs including detailed debugging information&#10; info: Show informational messages and above&#10; warn: Show warnings and errors only (default)&#10; error: Show errors only&#10; (must be one of [debug error info warn]) (default info)&#10; --logoutput enum set the log output destination&#10; stdout: Write logs to standard output&#10; stderr: Write logs to standard error, useful for separating logs from normal output&#10; (must be one of [stderr stdout]) (default stderr)&#10; --plugin-directory string default directory path for ocm plugins. (default &amp;#34;$HOME/.config/ocm/plugins&amp;#34;)&#10; --plugin-shutdown-timeout duration Timeout for plugin shutdown. If a plugin does not shut down within this time, it is forcefully killed (default 10s)&#10; --temp-folder string Specify a custom temporary folder path for filesystem operations.&#10; --working-directory string Specify a custom working directory path to load resources from.&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;h3 id="see-also"&gt;SEE ALSO&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm/"&gt;ocm&lt;/a&gt;&#9; - The official Open Component Model (OCM) CLI&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-download-plugin/"&gt;ocm download plugin&lt;/a&gt;&#9; - Download plugin binaries from a component version.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-download-resource/"&gt;ocm download resource&lt;/a&gt;&#9; - Download resources described in a component version in an OCM Repository&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;</description></item><item><title>ocm download plugin</title><link>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-download-plugin/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-download-plugin/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="ocm-download-plugin"&gt;ocm download plugin&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Download plugin binaries from a component version.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="synopsis"&gt;Synopsis&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Download a plugin binary from a component version located in a component version.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>ocm download resource</title><link>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-download-resource/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-download-resource/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="ocm-download-resource"&gt;ocm download resource&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Download resources described in a component version in an OCM Repository&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="synopsis"&gt;Synopsis&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Download a resource from a component version located in an Open Component Model (OCM) repository.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>ocm generate</title><link>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-generate/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-generate/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="ocm-generate"&gt;ocm generate&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Generate documentation for the OCM CLI&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="synopsis"&gt;Synopsis&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;A longer description that spans multiple lines and likely contains examples&#10;and usage of using your command. For example:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>ocm generate docs</title><link>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-generate-docs/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-generate-docs/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="ocm-generate-docs"&gt;ocm generate docs&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Generate Documentation for the CLI&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="synopsis"&gt;Synopsis&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Generate documentation for the OCM CLI in various formats, including Hugo-compatible markdown.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>ocm get</title><link>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-get/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-get/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="ocm-get"&gt;ocm get&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Get anything from OCM&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;div class="expressive-code"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figure class="frame not-content"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figcaption class="header"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;span class="title"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;ocm get {component-version|component-versions|cv|cvs|config|cfg} [flags]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;h3 id="options"&gt;Options&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;div class="expressive-code"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figure class="frame not-content"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figcaption class="header"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;span class="title"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt; -h, --help help for get&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;h3 id="options-inherited-from-parent-commands"&gt;Options inherited from parent commands&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;div class="expressive-code"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figure class="frame not-content"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figcaption class="header"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;span class="title"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt; --config stringArray supply configuration by a given configuration file.&#10; By default (without specifying custom locations with this flag), the file will be read from one of the well known locations:&#10; 1. The path specified in the OCM_CONFIG environment variable&#10; 2. The XDG_CONFIG_HOME directory (if set), or the default XDG home ($HOME/.config), or the user&amp;#39;s home directory&#10; - $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ocm/config&#10; - $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/.ocmconfig&#10; - $HOME/.config/ocm/config&#10; - $HOME/.config/.ocmconfig&#10; - $HOME/.ocm/config&#10; - $HOME/.ocmconfig&#10; 3. The current working directory:&#10; - $PWD/.ocm/config&#10; - $PWD/.ocmconfig&#10; 4. The directory of the current executable:&#10; - $EXE_DIR/.ocm/config&#10; - $EXE_DIR/.ocmconfig&#10; If multiple configuration files are found, they will be merged in the order they are discovered.&#10; Later entries have higher priority.&#10; Using the option, the specified configuration file(s) will be used instead of the lookup above.&#10; --logformat enum set the log output format that is used to print individual logs&#10; json: Output logs in JSON format, suitable for machine processing&#10; text: Output logs in human-readable text format, suitable for console output&#10; (must be one of [json text]) (default text)&#10; --loglevel enum sets the logging level&#10; debug: Show all logs including detailed debugging information&#10; info: Show informational messages and above&#10; warn: Show warnings and errors only (default)&#10; error: Show errors only&#10; (must be one of [debug error info warn]) (default info)&#10; --logoutput enum set the log output destination&#10; stdout: Write logs to standard output&#10; stderr: Write logs to standard error, useful for separating logs from normal output&#10; (must be one of [stderr stdout]) (default stderr)&#10; --plugin-directory string default directory path for ocm plugins. (default &amp;#34;$HOME/.config/ocm/plugins&amp;#34;)&#10; --plugin-shutdown-timeout duration Timeout for plugin shutdown. If a plugin does not shut down within this time, it is forcefully killed (default 10s)&#10; --temp-folder string Specify a custom temporary folder path for filesystem operations.&#10; --working-directory string Specify a custom working directory path to load resources from.&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;h3 id="see-also"&gt;SEE ALSO&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm/"&gt;ocm&lt;/a&gt;&#9; - The official Open Component Model (OCM) CLI&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-get-component-version/"&gt;ocm get component-version&lt;/a&gt;&#9; - Get component version(s) from an OCM repository&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-get-config/"&gt;ocm get config&lt;/a&gt;&#9; - Display the effective merged OCM configuration&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-get-types/"&gt;ocm get types&lt;/a&gt;&#9; - Describe OCM types and their configuration schema&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;</description></item><item><title>ocm get component-version</title><link>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-get-component-version/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-get-component-version/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="ocm-get-component-version"&gt;ocm get component-version&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Get component version(s) from an OCM repository&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="synopsis"&gt;Synopsis&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Get component version(s) from an OCM repository.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The format of a component reference is:&#10;[type::]{repository}/[valid-prefix]/{component}[:version]&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>ocm get config</title><link>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-get-config/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-get-config/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="ocm-get-config"&gt;ocm get config&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Display the effective merged OCM configuration&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="synopsis"&gt;Synopsis&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Evaluate the command line arguments and all explicitly or implicitly used&#10;configuration files and display the merged effective configuration as a single object.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>ocm get types</title><link>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-get-types/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-get-types/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="ocm-get-types"&gt;ocm get types&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Describe OCM types and their configuration schema&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="synopsis"&gt;Synopsis&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Describe OCM types registered in various subsystems.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;WHAT ARE SUBSYSTEMS?&#10;OCM uses a plugin-based architecture where different types of functionality are organized&#10;into subsystems. Each subsystem is a collection of related type implementations. When you&#10;use OCM commands or configure OCM resources, you specify types from these subsystems.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>ocm plugin</title><link>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-plugin/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-plugin/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="ocm-plugin"&gt;ocm plugin&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Manage OCM plugins&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;div class="expressive-code"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figure class="frame not-content"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figcaption class="header"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;span class="title"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;ocm plugin [flags]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;h3 id="options"&gt;Options&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;div class="expressive-code"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figure class="frame not-content"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figcaption class="header"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;span class="title"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt; -h, --help help for plugin&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;h3 id="options-inherited-from-parent-commands"&gt;Options inherited from parent commands&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&lt;div class="expressive-code"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figure class="frame not-content"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;figcaption class="header"&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;span class="title"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt; --config stringArray supply configuration by a given configuration file.&#10; By default (without specifying custom locations with this flag), the file will be read from one of the well known locations:&#10; 1. The path specified in the OCM_CONFIG environment variable&#10; 2. The XDG_CONFIG_HOME directory (if set), or the default XDG home ($HOME/.config), or the user&amp;#39;s home directory&#10; - $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ocm/config&#10; - $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/.ocmconfig&#10; - $HOME/.config/ocm/config&#10; - $HOME/.config/.ocmconfig&#10; - $HOME/.ocm/config&#10; - $HOME/.ocmconfig&#10; 3. The current working directory:&#10; - $PWD/.ocm/config&#10; - $PWD/.ocmconfig&#10; 4. The directory of the current executable:&#10; - $EXE_DIR/.ocm/config&#10; - $EXE_DIR/.ocmconfig&#10; If multiple configuration files are found, they will be merged in the order they are discovered.&#10; Later entries have higher priority.&#10; Using the option, the specified configuration file(s) will be used instead of the lookup above.&#10; --logformat enum set the log output format that is used to print individual logs&#10; json: Output logs in JSON format, suitable for machine processing&#10; text: Output logs in human-readable text format, suitable for console output&#10; (must be one of [json text]) (default text)&#10; --loglevel enum sets the logging level&#10; debug: Show all logs including detailed debugging information&#10; info: Show informational messages and above&#10; warn: Show warnings and errors only (default)&#10; error: Show errors only&#10; (must be one of [debug error info warn]) (default info)&#10; --logoutput enum set the log output destination&#10; stdout: Write logs to standard output&#10; stderr: Write logs to standard error, useful for separating logs from normal output&#10; (must be one of [stderr stdout]) (default stderr)&#10; --plugin-directory string default directory path for ocm plugins. (default &amp;#34;$HOME/.config/ocm/plugins&amp;#34;)&#10; --plugin-shutdown-timeout duration Timeout for plugin shutdown. If a plugin does not shut down within this time, it is forcefully killed (default 10s)&#10; --temp-folder string Specify a custom temporary folder path for filesystem operations.&#10; --working-directory string Specify a custom working directory path to load resources from.&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;h3 id="see-also"&gt;SEE ALSO&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm/"&gt;ocm&lt;/a&gt;&#9; - The official Open Component Model (OCM) CLI&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://ocm.software/0.13/docs/reference/ocm-cli/ocm-plugin-registry/"&gt;ocm plugin registry&lt;/a&gt;&#9; - Manage plugin registries&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>